# {{ .APP_NAME }}

A browser-based dictation app powered by [SpeechKit](https://speechkit.cc).
Records audio in the browser and transcribes it via
`POST /v1/dictation/transcribe` on the SpeechKit Server.

## Prerequisites

- Node 20+
- A running SpeechKit Server (default `{{ .SPEECHKIT_SERVER_URL }}`)
- (optional) Bearer token if the server uses `auth_mode = "bearer"`

## Configure

```sh
cp .env.example .env
# edit .env and adjust VITE_SPEECHKIT_SERVER_URL and VITE_SPEECHKIT_TOKEN
```

## Run

```sh
npm install
npm run dev
```

Then open <http://localhost:5173>, click **Start recording**, speak,
then click **Stop & transcribe**. The transcript appears in the textarea.

## How it works

`src/App.tsx` uses the browser `MediaRecorder` API to capture WebM/Opus
audio, then POSTs the blob to `/v1/dictation/transcribe` as `multipart/
form-data`. SpeechKit handles the format conversion server-side.
